  "worked_solution": "The standard equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nFor a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin, the equations of the asymptotes are\n\n$$\ny=\\pm \\frac{b}{a}x.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the given equation in standard form, we divide both sides of the equation by $144$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{x}^{2}-16{y}^{2} & =144 \\\\ \\frac{9{x}^{2}}{144}-\\frac{16{y}^{2}}{144} & =\\frac{144}{144} \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $a=\\sqrt{16}=4,$ and $b=\\sqrt{9}=3.$ \n\nTherefore, the asymptotes are $y=\\pm \\frac{3}{4}x.$",
